    "module": {
      "summary": "Pensions Act 2014 s.4 — entitlement to state pension at the transitional\nrate.\n\nA person reaches entitlement when\n  s.4(1)(a): they have reached pensionable age,\n  s.4(1)(b): they have at least the minimum qualifying years (regs max 10),\n  s.4(1)(c): they have at least one pre-commencement qualifying year.\n\ns.4(4) defines a pre-commencement qualifying year as either\n  * a qualifying year starting 1978-04-06 ≤ year_start < 2016-04-06, OR\n  * a reckonable year deemed qualifying under SI 1979/643 reg 13(1).\n\nThe \"pre/post commencement\" classification is a date-range test the\ncaller pre-applies on each QualifyingYear record as\n`is_pre_commencement_qy` and `is_post_commencement_qy` so the filtered\n`count_where` aggregator can count them without needing the deployed\nDSL to evaluate date comparisons inside an aggregation predicate."
    },
